.TH MAKE\-NODE\-CONFIGS 1 "September 2026" "mu2edaq-diskwatcher 1.3.0" "Mu2e DAQ Utilities"
.SH NAME
make\-node\-configs.sh \- generate one mu2edaq\-diskwatcher configuration per DAQ node
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tools/make\-node\-configs.sh
[\fB\-n\fR]
[\fB\-f\fR]
[\fB\-o\fR \fIDIR\fR]
[\fB\-t\fR \fIFILE\fR]
[\fB\-d\fR \fIDOMAIN\fR]
[\fIHOST\fR ...]
.br
.B tools/make\-node\-configs.sh
.B \-l
.SH DESCRIPTION
Writes
.IR config/nodes/mu2e\-diskwatcher\- node .yaml
for each DAQ node from the template
.BR config/nodes/node.template.yaml ,
substituting the node's name into the header comment and into the pid and log
file names.
The nodes all watch the same six areas
.RB ( /data ", " /daqlogs ", " /scratch ", " /var ", " /var/log ", " /tmp )
with the same free-space thresholds, so a threshold change is one edit to the
template and one run of this script rather than the same edit in every file.
.PP
With no
.I HOST
arguments the built-in Mu2e list is used:
.BR mu2egateway01 ", " mu2egateway02 ", " mu2e\-dl\-02 ", " mu2e\-cfo\-01 ", "
.BR mu2e\-trk\-01 " through " mu2e\-trk\-14 ", " mu2e\-calo\-01 " through "
.BR mu2e\-calo\-08 " and " mu2e\-crv\-01 .
.B mu2e\-dl\-01
is deliberately absent: it keeps its hand-written
.BR config/mu2e\-diskwatcher\-dl\-01.yaml ,
which also watches system logs and
.BR /home .
.PP
A generated file carries a
.B GENERATED
line in its header.
A file at the target path without that line is taken to have been edited by
hand and is skipped, so a deliberate local change is never silently lost;
.B \-\-force
overwrites it anyway.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-dry\-run
Print what would be written and write nothing.
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-force
Overwrite hand-edited files.
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-output " " \fIDIR\fR
Output directory.
Default:
.BR config/nodes .
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-template " " \fIFILE\fR
Template to substitute into.
Default:
.BR config/nodes/node.template.yaml .
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-domain " " \fIDOMAIN\fR
Domain appended to short names in the header.
Default:
.BR fnal.gov .
.TP
.BR \-a ", " \-\-aggregator " " \fIHOST\fR
Also write
.IR config/mu2e\-diskwatcher\- short .yaml
for the aggregator node
.I HOST
from
.BR config/nodes/aggregator.template.yaml ,
with every node (and
.BR mu2e\-dl\-01 ,
never
.I HOST
itself) listed under
.B peers.static
and under
.BR peers.discover.probe .
Default:
.BR mu2e\-mgr\-01 .
.B \-\-no\-aggregator
skips it.
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-list
Print the built-in node list, one per line, and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print usage and exit.
.SH TEMPLATE PLACEHOLDERS
.TP
.B @HOST@
Short hostname, e.g.
.BR mu2e\-trk\-03 .
.TP
.B @FQDN@
.IR HOST . DOMAIN .
.TP
.B @FILE@
The output file name, e.g.
.BR mu2e\-diskwatcher\-trk\-03.yaml .
.TP
.B @FILE_STEM@
The file name without
.BR .yaml ,
used for the pid and log names inside the per-node run directory.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B config/nodes/node.template.yaml
The template.
.TP
.B config/nodes/mu2e\-diskwatcher\-*.yaml
The generated configurations.
.TP
.B config/nodes/aggregator.template.yaml
The aggregator template; its
.B @STATIC_PEERS@
and
.B @PROBE_HOSTS@
lines are replaced by the node lists.
.TP
.B config/mu2e\-diskwatcher\-mgr\-01.yaml
The generated aggregator configuration.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Every requested file was written (or, with
.BR \-n ,
listed).
.TP
.B 1
Bad option, or the template does not exist.
.TP
.B 2
At least one file was skipped as hand-edited.
.SH EXAMPLES
Regenerate every node file after changing a threshold in the template:
.PP
.nf
    tools/make\-node\-configs.sh
.fi
.PP
Add a node that is not in the built-in list:
.PP
.nf
    tools/make\-node\-configs.sh mu2e\-trk\-15
.fi
.PP
Start the watcher on a node with its generated file:
.PP
.nf
    ./start\-mu2edaq\-diskwatcher.sh \-c config/nodes/mu2e\-diskwatcher\-trk\-03.yaml
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mu2edaq\-diskwatcher (1),
.BR mu2edaq\-diskwatcher.conf (5)
